From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Maicon Alves <alvesmaiconn@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 02:03:09 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 40/40] client: a near block left without its detail mesh gets
 it back

The culler asks for the detail mesh of a block left out as far only when its traversal reaches
the block; one it never reaches, behind a wall whose own mesh is missing too, stays a hole. The
touch of the blocks in range, every four seconds, now asks for the detail mesh of any block left
out that is within the detail distance, as the loops culler already did on every draw list.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>

diff --git a/src/client/clientmap.cpp b/src/client/clientmap.cpp
index 386e2e497..f16197ec0 100644
--- a/src/client/clientmap.cpp
+++ b/src/client/clientmap.cpp
@@ -1015,6 +1015,14 @@ void ClientMap::touchMapBlocks()
 
 			blocks_in_range++;
 
+			// Left without its detail mesh while it counted as far: asked again once it is near
+			if (block->detail_mesh == MapBlock::DetailMesh::LeftOut && m_cache_lod_distance > 0 &&
+					lodDistance(getContainerPos(block->getPos(), LodMeshGenerator::REGION) * LodMeshGenerator::REGION) <=
+					(m_cache_lod_distance + LOD_DETAIL_MARGIN) * BS) {
+				block->detail_mesh = MapBlock::DetailMesh::Asked;
+				m_client->addUpdateMeshTask(block->getPos());
+			}
+
 			if (m_cache_unload_out_of_view) {
 				// Out of view: let it expire like a block out of range
 				v3f to_block = mesh_sphere_center - m_camera_position;
